        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Trey Anastasio, Sarah Nixey\n- Organizations: Phish, Trey Anastasio Band, Black Box Recorder, New York Philharmonic, Los Angeles Philharmonic, Atlanta Symphony Orchestra, Baltimore Symphony, Pittsburgh Symphony, Colorado Symphony\n- Products: The Horseshoe Curve, Sing, Memory\n\nFacts:\n- Trey Anastasio was born on September 30, 1964.\n- Sarah Nixey was born on December 21, 1973, in Dorset, England.\n- Trey Anastasio is an American guitarist, composer, and vocalist noted for his work with Phish and for his solo career.\n- Trey Anastasio's solo career includes the Trey Anastasio Band and the orchestral \"Evenings with Trey Anastasio\" performed with the New York Philharmonic, Los Angeles Philharmonic, Atlanta Symphony Orchestra, Baltimore Symphony, Pittsburgh Symphony, and Colorado Symphony.\n- Sarah Nixey is a British singer-songwriter best known as the vocalist in Black Box Recorder.\n- The Horseshoe Curve is Trey Anastasio's sixth studio album.\n- Sing, Memory is the debut album by Sarah Nixey.",
